sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task + full intent as inputs, single-swamp-node; DECISIONS 1 (token minted at admission, vault.get), 3 (automatic deploy = Gateway-published native schedule, no POST back), 4 / R1-R4 (process.stop shape); .env through the vault as in instance.create; rule 7 (reload over restart, restart_on_deploy only). docs/reference/deployments.md.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 21, 22 (automatic deploys only in instance.auto_deploy; cfgmgmt file/link/systemd, 0600 credential file for the fetch).
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: instance:deploy
  %% kind: instance.deploy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Instance Node<br/>Node 12 over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:deploy 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:deploy 42`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--commit=SHA] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Instance; without `--commit`, the newest commit of its deployment branch
  %%> - `--commit`: a full commit SHA that must be on the branch's first-parent chain
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  %%> - automatic deploys start the same deploy steps from a native schedule; see the `instance.auto_deploy` chart
  opt Development default in a container
    Note over GW: Capture source facts<br/>project:update capture
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the requested commit, or the default branch head once; freezes that SHA for the run
    %%> - checks the Instance migration before reading; reads outside the write transaction; admission rechecks migration, source configuration and idempotency
    %%> - capture or classification failure refuses admission; see /reference/deployments#container-source-facts
  end
  Note over GW: Validate, freeze intent<br/>Instance 42 locked · task #5150
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active Instance of Project 7 on an app-prod or app-dev Node
  %%> - a pending default Route projection refuses `deployment.projection_pending`; successful container create or migration completes that projection with its seed
  %%> - no other operation holds Instance 42; else `operation.target_busy`
  %%> Freezes:
  %%> - the branch and commit, the deploy steps, the shared paths and the release name
  %%> - the Project's Process and Schedule definitions and the PHP runtime
  %%> - the account `orbit-app-7` and its home `/home/orbit-app-7`
  %%> Renders .env:
  %%> - from the stored environment of Instance 42
  %%> Result:
  %%> - deployment 88 recorded as running; task #5150 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - a manual production deploy pauses automatic deployment of Instance 42
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Push token and .env<br/>vault: github-token, env-5150
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the repository is private, and only the Gateway holds the GitHub App key
  %%> - `.env` can hold secrets, which travel only through the vault
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - mints a read token for this one repository, valid 1 hour; confirmed public repositories remain readable anonymously
  %%> - credential preparation refuses source.github_app_denied before writing the fetch credential, naming the App and owner/repository; install the App or add the repository
  %%> - source.github_unavailable means GitHub could not supply a credential; it never becomes an empty credential
  %%> - pushes the token and the rendered `.env` into Swamp's vault
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the run reads both with `vault.get`; no step calls the Gateway back
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-deploy-direct
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one run on Swamp serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the frozen intent; secrets only as vault key names
  %%> Budget:
  %%> - the sum of the deploy step timeouts plus 900 s
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5150
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task until it ends
  opt Development checkout
    SW->>N: Write the fetch credential<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Fetch the branch<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Remove fetch credential<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Check tracked changes<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Resolve the commit<br/>ssh exec argv
    opt --commit
      SW->>N: Count commits after it<br/>ssh exec argv
      SW->>N: Read the branch ancestor<br/>ssh exec argv
      Note over SW: Check it is on the branch<br/>native assert
    end
    SW->>N: Read the local branch<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Check the local branch<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: List untracked entries<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: List target directories<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: Plan the cleanup<br/>typed data
    SW->>N: Check the checkout lock<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Clean stale directories<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Check out the commit<br/>ssh exec argv
  end
  opt Development default in a container
    Note over SW: Write the container intent<br/>ansible-input
    SW->>N: Start the container<br/>Ansible · tags start
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts a stopped default container; see docs/cli/instance/container/deploy-default.mmd
    opt nested-fleet default
      SW->>N: Check the inner fleet<br/>Ansible · tags fleet_check
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - compares the inner fleet with its rules and changes nothing; refuses `instance.container_fleet_drift` before the seed, so nothing is restored
      SW->>N: Keep the current seed<br/>Ansible · tags seed
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - retakes the seed of the default as it is, fleet included, so a failed refresh never restores a seed from before the fleet
    end
    SW->>N: Fetch into the mirror<br/>Ansible · tags fetch
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - fetches into the Node's mirror with the read token and pushes the branch into the container as a bundle
    %%> - a pinned commit off the branch's first-parent chain refuses `deployment.commit_not_on_branch`
    SW->>N: Check out in the container<br/>Ansible · tags checkout
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - refuses tracked changes with `deployment.checkout_dirty` and a branch the commit does not fast-forward with `deployment.branch_diverged`
    SW->>N: Run dev deploy steps<br/>incus exec · vault copy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - each Project command as `orbit` in the workspace, with the runtime folder's PATH
    SW->>N: Install the Processes<br/>Ansible · tags processes
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes changed `orbit-*` units and new environment files from the vault, removes former ones, and restarts the changed units
    %%> - the seed snapshot then restarts every running Process on the new commit
    opt nested-fleet default
      SW->>N: Start the inner fleet<br/>Ansible · tags fleet_start
      SW->>N: Refresh the inner fleet<br/>Ansible · tags fleet_refresh
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - only an intent with `fleet` runs them: docs/cli/instance/container/fleet-refresh.mmd
    end
    SW->>N: Take the seed snapshot<br/>Ansible · tags seed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stops the units, snapshots `seed-<commit>`, starts them again and deletes older seeds
    %%> - a nested-fleet default retakes it at the same commit, and refuses a Club key file on its disk
    SW->>N: Check the container<br/>Ansible · tags check
    opt nested-fleet default failed after checkout
      SW->>N: Restore the old seed<br/>Ansible · fleet_restore
      SW->>N: Start on the old seed<br/>Ansible · tags start
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - puts the default back on its newest seed and starts it; the failed phase's result stays the run's result
    end
    Note over SW: Read the container result<br/>result file
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the deployed commit, or the public code of the refusal
    Note over SW: Remove the run folder<br/>always
  end
  opt Production release
    SW->>N: Write release credential<br/>cfgmgmt/file apply
    SW->>N: Prepare the release<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Remove release credential<br/>cfgmgmt/file apply
    SW->>N: Read the release commit<br/>ssh exec argv
    opt --commit
      SW->>N: Read first-parent chain<br/>ssh exec argv
      Note over SW: Check the branch commit<br/>native assert
    end
    SW->>N: Prepare shared paths<br/>ssh exec argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - seeds only empty persistent directories and links the admitted shared paths after the branch check
    SW->>N: Link the release<br/>cfgmgmt/link apply
    SW->>N: Read the key names<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: Check for foreign keys<br/>native assert
    SW->>N: Create the orbit-env group<br/>cfgmgmt/group apply
    SW->>N: Write .env<br/>cfgmgmt/file apply
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the Instance account writes `.env` as `0640` in its home, so no root write follows a link it placed
    SW->>N: Set the group orbit-env<br/>ssh exec argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - root runs `chgrp -h orbit-env` on the written files, which never follows a link, so the Node agent may read the key names
  end
  opt Deploy steps need Vite+
    SW->>N: dev-vp-read-package<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: dev-vp-read-pnpm_lock<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: dev-vp-read-npm_lock<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: dev-vp-read-node_version<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: dev-vp-read-nvmrc<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: dev-vp-home<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: dev-vp-store<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: dev-vp-links<br/>typed data
    SW->>N: dev-vp-read-workspace<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: dev-vp-requirements<br/>typed data
    SW->>N: Read Vite manager home<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Read Vite manager CLI<br/>cfgmgmt/file check
    SW->>N: dev-vp-manager<br/> run
    Note over SW: dev-vp-manager-ready<br/>native assert
    SW->>N: Prepare Vite cache<br/>cfgmgmt/directory apply
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - gives the production account its own cache; the Node manager still supplies the shared CLI
    SW->>N: Publish public Vite CLI<br/>ssh exec argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - publishes only the managed standalone binary; compare skips an unchanged copy, and no private manager data is copied
    SW->>N: dev-vp-cli<br/>ssh exec argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the CLI version; the first invocation also bootstraps the app's private cache
    Note over SW: dev-vp-cli-ready<br/>typed data
    SW->>N: dev-vp-install<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: dev-vp-inventory<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: dev-vp-verify<br/>typed data
    Note over SW: dev-vp-result<br/>typed data
  end
  opt Development deploy steps
    SW->>N: Run the deploy steps<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Read the checkout branch<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Read the checkout commit<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: Check the checkout<br/>native assert
  end
  opt Production activation
    SW->>N: Run before steps<br/>ssh exec argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs each frozen private command as the Project account in the new release; later required commands stop after a failure
    SW->>N: Grant Caddy access<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Activate release<br/>cfgmgmt/link apply
    SW->>N: Swap current<br/>ssh exec argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - atomically renames current.next over current; failure before this point keeps the earlier selection
    SW->>N: Prepare PHP directories<br/>cfgmgmt/directory apply
    SW->>N: Read local PHP tuning<br/>cfgmgmt/file check
    SW->>N: Write PHP configuration<br/>cfgmgmt/file apply
    SW->>N: Write default PHP tuning<br/>cfgmgmt/file apply
    %%> When:
    %%> - the dedicated runtime has no local tuning file; existing operator settings stay intact
    SW->>N: Test PHP configuration<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Start PHP runtime<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd apply
    SW->>N: Refresh PHP cache<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Check PHP runtime<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd check
    SW->>N: Install Processes<br/> run
    SW->>N: Read Schedule group<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: Render Schedules<br/>typed data
    SW->>N: Write Schedule services<br/>cfgmgmt/file apply
    SW->>N: Install Schedule timers<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd apply
    SW->>N: Read Schedule timers<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd check
    Note over SW: Check Schedule timers<br/>native assert
    SW->>N: Restart Processes<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Run after steps<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Find releases in use<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Clean up releases<br/>ssh exec argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes only releases outside the retained three, after checking no process uses them; cleanup failure is a warning
    SW->>N: Read current back<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Check Process state<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd check
    SW->>N: Read container state<br/>ssh exec argv
    SW->>N: Read deployed commit<br/>ssh exec argv
    Note over SW: Check the deployment<br/>native assert
  end
  alt all required steps pass
    N-->>SW: release, commit
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the selected release and its commit, and the restarted Processes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the outputs; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the deployment<br/>release, commit · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - deployment 88 succeeds with its release and commit
    %%> - task #5150 succeeds
  else a required step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - a required step exits with an error, SSH fails, or the budget runs out
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed_step, selected release
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its safe error code; private command output is suppressed
    %%> - which release `current` selects now
    Note over GW: Record failed deployment<br/>selection kept · task failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - deployment 88 is marked failed; task #5150 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a failure before activation keeps the old release selected
    %%> - a failure after activation keeps the new release selected
    %%> - Orbit undoes no step and no data change; the new release folder stays until a cleanup
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - deploy again after a fix; it is a new task with a new release
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5150
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status until it has ended
    %%> - the CLI uses Reverb events when the `websocket` role is active
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
